So one of the reasons

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:26.072
the candidates are not out there

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.907
quite as much this week

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:28.941
and next is because it's

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.610
almost the end of the second quarter

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.377
for fundraising.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.079
So it's a critical time for fundraising.

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:33.412
But look,

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:34.981
if they wanted to be out there

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:35.548
making noise,

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.216
they certainly know how to do that.

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:37.817
A run as it is

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:40.419
will be in Nevada over the weekend.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:41.554
We'll see if he says anything

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:41.921
at that point.

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.322
But look, they're all sort of tiptoeing

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.590
to see where they're going.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.992
But there is a lane in a market

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:48.661
among some Republicans for

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:49.762
someone to stand up for this.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:51.163
Well, see if anyone steps into it.

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:53.232
Boy, do you have my card here.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:54.700
You exactly just tweeted it

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.903
right up for me. It's really amazing.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:58.871
Let's hear from Chris Christie

00:08:58.871 --> 00:08:59.438
because I feel like

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.741
because it was so much news yesterday,

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:03.209
this is very telling

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:04.110
to what you're talking about,

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.211
what he told Anderson

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:06.646
and CNN's town hall Monday night.

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:09.482
Why do you think they're not addressing

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:10.650
what's actually in the indictment?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.852
Because it's indefensible

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:13.953
and they're playing games.

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:16.455
Look, you all need to know this.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.692
They're playing political games with you

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.328
because they think you kind of like Trump

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:23.296
a little bit.

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.498
And I don't see anything bad about Trump.

00:09:25.498 --> 00:09:26.132
And then Trump

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:27.833
kind of implodes and goes away.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.037
Then you're more likely to vote for me.

00:09:31.037 --> 00:09:33.339
And then another roadmap for Republicans.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:34.640
Most Republicans,

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.341
a lot of

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:37.043
Americans read The Wall Street Journal,

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:38.344
but it's known for its conservative

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:39.312
editorial board

00:09:39.312 --> 00:09:40.546
last week, a destructive

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:41.280
Trump indictment.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.048
Do prosecutors

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:43.950
understand the forces they're unleashing?

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.685
But yesterday, last night,

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:47.720
the destructive Donald Trump

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.890
the document indictment is misguided, but

00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:52.992
he makes it easier for his enemies,

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:55.261
as he always does.

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.796
Self-destructive Trump.

00:09:56.796 --> 00:09:58.531
I mean, that is a bumper sticker message

00:09:58.531 --> 00:09:59.732
if you ever heard one.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:00.366
Of course, The Wall Street

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:01.167
Journal editorial page

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:02.668
has been editorializing against Trump

00:10:02.668 --> 00:10:03.603
for quite some time.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.404
But it is something that shows you

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:06.706
that there is an audience

00:10:06.706 --> 00:10:07.740
and a lane for this.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.775
So we will see come August

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:11.677
when that first debate happens.

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.213
How many Republican rivals and candidates

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.182
are willing to take that step?

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:16.916
That'll tell us a lot.

